{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted","id":1056425,"title":"Would this be Weaver or Wyld tainted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-28T19:49:57-08:00","id":1056425,"title":"Would this be Weaver or Wyld tainted?","content":"I have a question. I thought up a interesting storyhook where a corporation called Prism is doing a top secret project to create what they call &quot; a new Garden of Eden&quot; . My question is will this project reek of the Wyld or Weaver ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T19:59:46-08:00","id":1056429,"title":"","content":"I guess I would need to know more of the project details. With that kinda name it could go both ways really","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T19:59:49-08:00","id":1056430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted#post1056425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...a corporation...top secret project...</div> </div> </div> </div>Weaver, almost certainly. Unless they open a portal to Pangaia or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T20:13:53-08:00","id":1056442,"title":"","content":"Basically the project is being headed by a botanist named Nigel Carlswell, a Englishmen. This project is taking place on a island in the South Pacific where Prism sent a staff of scientists, security personal and God knows what else there to begin research. They are basically working on a way to make a island as bountiful as The Garden of Eden and possibly make a artificial ecosystem able to sustain life. I figured making life would be a Wyld thing. But, the ways of making that life is probably of the Weaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T20:17:07-08:00","id":1056445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1056442#post1056442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically the project is being headed by a botanist named Nigel Carlswell, a Englishmen. This project is taking place on a island in the South Pacific where Prism sent a staff of scientists, security personal and God knows what else there to begin research. They are basically working on a way to make a island as bountiful as The Garden of Eden and possibly make a artificial ecosystem able to sustain life. I figured making life would be a Wyld thing. But, the ways of making that life is probably of the Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would probably be both","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T20:25:52-08:00","id":1056448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1056445#post1056445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would probably be both</div> </div> </div> </div>So, some kind of dual Weaver- Wyld taint? I wonder if that could work. I am also wondering how Werewolves and other shapechangers would react to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T20:32:21-08:00","id":1056449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1056448#post1056448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, some kind of dual Weaver- Wyld taint? I wonder if that could work. I am also wondering how Werewolves and other shapechangers would react to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, vampires are Weaver-Wyrm, so, I see no problem with that.<br /> <br /> The Fera would probably have mixed fellings about it, but I bet most of them wouldn't look too favorably to it. However, as the world becomes ever more shittier, they may see it as a great chance to create something capable do hold the Wyrm at bay, s\u00f3. The","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T20:53:33-08:00","id":1056452,"title":"","content":"The Storm Eater of the Wyld West was a very powerful spirit made of the merging of a great Weaver spirit and a huge Bane. It was unequivocally an enemy of the North American Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T21:07:42-08:00","id":1056457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1056452#post1056452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Storm Eater of the Wyld West was a very powerful spirit made of the merging of a great Weaver spirit and a huge Bane. It was unequivocally an enemy of the North American Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, would that mean mixing Weaver and Wyld taint would make most fera see this project as a abomination? Also, Prism is a corporation that does agriculture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T22:09:34-08:00","id":1056484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1056457#post1056457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, would that mean mixing Weaver and Wyld taint would make most fera see this project as a abomination? Also, Prism is a corporation that does agriculture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. The Glasswalkers would be all for it. Children of Gaia (well, &quot;a&quot; Child of Gaia) have done something similar before (with terrible consequences, but they did try).<br /> <br /> Personally I think you'd have a good third of the Tribes interested at the very least. Mind you, they may not want humans meddling in things like this and might try and get some kinfolk working in there is initial investigations (by Garou) revealed the company was on the up and up.<br /> <br /> Worth remembering: Most things in the world are made up of degrees of &quot;taint&quot; from varying members of the Triat.<br /> Also, most Garou don't go around sensing for Wyld or Weaver taint. They don't usually have the abilities (Gifts) to do so. Some Camps here and there had specific Gifts for it, but they weren't terribly common. Some of the other Fera had Sense Triat and Sense Weaver and Sense Wyld Gifts though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T05:36:39-08:00","id":1056584,"title":"","content":"There are probably going to be three interested Tribes. Bone Gnawers would be interested because they are the sea dogs of the Garou, so they love traveling between the Pacific Islands. Children of Gaia are interested because of the potential for teaching humans to appreciate Gaia. Glass Walkers would be interested because it uses technology to improve the environment. You will also have Rokea interested in the project.<br /> <br /> Of course, the problem is that practically every Pacific Island of decent size is a Garden of Eden. I would suggest changing the location to the Desolation Islands (Kerguelen Islands) of the Indian Ocean instead. They are one of the most isolated places of Earth, they are pretty barren, and no one lives there permanently. It is also on the equivalent latitude as Paris, which shows you how important ocean currents are to habitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T06:09:53-08:00","id":1056598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1056442#post1056442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...botanist...staff of scientists...security personal...research...artificial ecosystem...</div> </div> </div> </div>Weaver...Weaver...Weaver...Weaver...Weaver...<br /> <br /> &quot;Life&quot; is not inherently Wyld. Life is just life. <i>Manufacturing</i> life is <i>Weaver</i>. Farms, Gardens, Greenhouses, Botanical Gardens, these are all more Weaver than Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":707,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","user":"etherial","date":". 03-01-2017, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:24:57-08:00","id":1056765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1056598#post1056598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaver...Weaver...Weaver...Weaver...Weaver...<br /> <br /> &quot;Life&quot; is not inherently Wyld. Life is just life. <i>Manufacturing</i> life is <i>Weaver</i>. Farms, Gardens, Greenhouses, Botanical Gardens, these are all more Weaver than Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. Well, i am sure the Weaver's involvement in this would attract some fera. I was thinking about three possible twists for this storyline.<br /> One: The scientists are using the Abyss to travel back in time to gather rare plants for their garden, unaware of the damage they might cause in the process..<br /> Two: They are tearing holes in the Umbra and are trying to recruit plant spirits to help them.<br /> Three: This is secretly a Shinzui plot.<br /> Which one do you like more?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T14:50:51-08:00","id":1056809,"title":"","content":"The first is impossible, the second is improbable, and the third is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:59:41-08:00","id":1056857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1056809#post1056809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first is impossible, the second is improbable, and the third is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the Abyss one, I figured that was possible due to Shattered Dreams. The Shinzui plot Idea is probably gonna be a theory that is thrown around by PCs. I was also thinking of including a drone that is either head of security or a scientist. Also, the Desolate Islands are near Madagascar so wouldn't that attract Africa's shapeshifters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:41:11-08:00","id":1056880,"title":"","content":"It is the most remote place on Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:51:03-08:00","id":1056888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1056880#post1056880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is the most remote place on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the scientists probably won't get much visitors. So, does that make the security forces pointless?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T20:19:16-08:00","id":1056960,"title":"","content":"Well, it depends on if their research is public or secret, and if they understand that there are supernatural threats. The Desolation Islands are under the authority of the French government, but the only people stationed there are around 100 administrators and scientists during the summer and around 40 people during the winter (there are more humans on the South Pole during the same season). It would be very easy to establish a secret base especially if the French government gave you it's blessings.<br /> <br /> The facility would be devoted to the 'Garden of Eden' project, but the location would be ideal for research into genetically engineered plants and plant diseases (such as bioweapons designed to destroy enemy food crops or artificial viruses that mutate enemy food crops into producing toxins). If the facility is used for military purposes as well as civilian purposes, you could have as many security personnel as research personnel.<br /> <br /> I would suggest a secret civilian-military research facility with French authorization. The base would use geothermal energy from Mont Ross (a local volcano), allowing it to minimize its fueling requirements. With 1,000 personnel year-round, it has 100 administrative personnel, 400 security personnel, 400 research personnel, and 100 support personnel during the summer and 1/5 that amount during the winter (a caretaker population). Personnel are rotated every six months and are subjected to a communication blackout during that time (only emergency and official communications are allowed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T02:21:12-08:00","id":1057028,"title":"","content":"Not everything needs to be defined by the Triat, though. It can easily be its own thing without any additional conotations. The fallout from it on the other hand could take all sorts of delightful mayhem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T05:32:41-08:00","id":1057056,"title":"","content":"I agree, though they will 'smell' of the Triat at the extremes. A secret research lab doing genetic engineering of advanced bioweapons is probably going to bear a hint of the Wyrm. Of course, how much depends of how much the mutation of plants matters depends on the ST, but I would suggest that research into plant diseases would create an unwholesome spiritual atmosphere.<br /> <br /> If you decide to go with the Desolation Islands, you will be 2,000 miles from the nearest inhabited area (Madagascar), so any spiritual taint will likely go unnoticed by the land dwelling Fera (unless it directly threatens Sea, Rokea will not care or notice). The Wyrm will notice though, so the personnel could start to exposed to Wyrm Taint while at the facility. If people associated with the specific company start coming back from a unspecified research center as Wyrm Tainted, then the Fera might notice. The Desolation Islands are a long way off of the beaten track though, so it might be a quest to get there before something really bad happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T08:59:43-08:00","id":1057114,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> You keep bringing up this pretty massive change to the original idea. It's not that it's a bad suggestion, but you're pushing it pretty hard as if it's the only viable or reasonable option (it's perfectly fine to keep the story in the Pacific; as with any setting, making it work is in the execution). So far, I've heard more of your ideas for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12186\" data-vbnamecard=\"12186\">Killerclown</a> 's story than I've heard of their own. You sure you don't want to just run it yourself? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Truly, though, there's nothing wrong with setting the story in the Pacific. Not every island is a lush &quot;Garden of Eden&quot; already. However, if you start on one, then you have something to build on. If you don't, then you have the advantage of making it from scratch. Either way, it sounds like the goal is a controlled environment, which is obviously not the way tropical Pacific islands are.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, it's not my story, so I've got no stake in the final product. It's just kinda weird to push your own agenda that hard on someone else's project when they came asking for advice and not an overhaul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T11:08:01-08:00","id":1057161,"title":"","content":"It is also worth saying (I think) that there is absolutely nothing stopping <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12186\" data-vbnamecard=\"12186\">Killerclown</a> from putting that exact island setup in the Pacific. It's the WoD, it doesn't need to map over 100% to the real world. So if it helps the story the Desolation Islands can be off the coast of Madagascar or Japan or Indonesia. They can be the exact same islands, or they can be islands with the exact same conditions. Plop them down wherever is helpful to the story. Ultimately, this seems like a less than vital detail since the focus is supposed to be the facility itself and the research they're doing there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T12:43:28-08:00","id":1057195,"title":"","content":"I am not a huge fan of time travel, but given the outline provided by Shattered Dreams, the Abyss does offer that as an option. If Pentex can have goons hunting dinosaurs in the Jurassic period, why not have some other similarly well-equipped scientists doing... botany...<br /> <br /> It makes sense to base this operation in a remote location, like some desolate island. Maybe the corp. is concerned about seeds escaping confinement or anachronistic diseases compromising the samples. It might even be that their project isn't bad in and of itself, maybe they are trying their best to solve world hunger or preserve extinct plant species.<br /> <br /> The conflict arises when the constant journeys through the sphincter of the Abyss draw the attention of vile things lurking in the gulf. Given that the humans don't really understand that they are dealing with the spirit world (rather than a 'temporal anomaly' or however they explain it), the token security could be overrun and possessed or mutated, and the away teams gathering their precious samples become stranded. It might be a real mess... and a fun/challenging scenario for some Garou and Fera to solve!<br /> <br /> Edit: and as far as roping in your players, having strange dreams come to either the pack or their elders is always an option. Unusual messengers via spirits, Corax or even Kami would also be good attention-getters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 03-02-2017, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:12:08-08:00","id":1057244,"title":"","content":"Well, as mentioned in a previous thread, Shattered Dreams is not canon, so the ST does not have to allow time travel. Anyway, how do normal humans cross the Gauntlet, travel across the Penumbra to the Abyss, descend the Abyss, survive in the past long enough to get a sample, climb up the Abyss, cross the Penumbra, and cross the Gaunlet? That would be a challenging feat for a group of Rank 5 Fera, much less a group of normal mortals. Though you could possibly have a natural portal to Pangaea, and the researchers mistakenly believe that they have done time travel...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:24:47-08:00","id":1057253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057244#post1057244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Though you could possibly have a natural portal to Pangaea, and the researchers mistakenly believe that they have done time travel...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was in the middle of typing pretty much this. I think Pangea is a better option than actual time travel.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:30:57-08:00","id":1057256,"title":"","content":"How would the scientists get to Pangea ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":".  Mistake on umbra placement 03-02-2017, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:37:21-08:00","id":1057257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057244#post1057244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as mentioned in a previous thread, Shattered Dreams is not canon, so the ST does not have to allow time travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>OP himself said he is interested in time travel. Like I said, not my cup of tea, but he brought it up, so I am gonna go there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057244#post1057244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Anyway, how do normal humans cross the Gauntlet, travel across the Penumbra to the Abyss, descend the Abyss, survive in the past long enough to get a sample, climb up the Abyss, cross the Penumbra, and cross the Gaunlet? That would be a challenging feat for a group of Rank 5 Fera, much less a group of normal mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a few blanks need to be filled in, but that isn't as impossible as you make it out out be. I don't know how Pentex is supposed to have done it, but they did, with some degree of regularity and efficiency. Replace Pentex with Prism (or whatever organization you want) and instead of of a Pentex-run Jurassic Park we've got something more akin to the Svalbard Seed Vault stocked with ancient plants; odd, but it certainly isn't the worst idea mashup ever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057244#post1057244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Though you could possibly have a natural portal to Pangaea, and the researchers mistakenly believe that they have done time travel...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure why Pangea is on the table, but the Abyss is off-limits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 03-02-2017, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:41:04-08:00","id":1057260,"title":"","content":"Well, a lot of it is ST fiat. Pangaea is the Primordial Realm of the Middle Umbra. A natural portal, only accessible from a specific location, could bridge the 'worlds' (it would also have to transform ephemera to life, but that is hardly a problem for a magic portal). The key to activating it could be anything (sonic vibrations, laser emissions, gravitational tides, etc). <br /> <br /> It would be interesting if it only opened for an hour at the apex of every full moon, meaning that teams would be stuck in Pangaea for four weeks. Garou could stumble on the team on a quest in Pangaea and would be terribly confused. The scientists would be equally confused when they encountered the Garou (if they do not end up gibbering in fear).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:42:32-08:00","id":1057261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057256#post1057256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the scientists get to Pangea ?</div> </div> </div> </div>How do <i>you</i> want them to get to Pangea? Do you want it to have been convoluted, involving magick or the aid of other supernaturals? Or do you want a group of surveyors to stumble upon a hidden gateway into a distant realm, misunderstand what they have found, and start trying to take advantage of their circumstances? What makes for a better story, in your mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T15:32:10-08:00","id":1057293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057257#post1057257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not sure why Pangea is on the table, but the Abyss is off-limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>It had occurred to me because one of the Mage books treated Pangea (well, Hollow Earth I think. Seemed like the same place) as being physically accessible. I kind of like the idea of having rare spots in the world where humans can wander in and dinosaurs can occasionally wander out.<br /> <br /> In any case, it seemed a lot more reasonable than the whole time travel/going down through the Abyss thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057260#post1057260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It would be interesting if it only opened for an hour at the apex of every full moon, meaning that teams would be stuck in Pangaea for four weeks. Garou could stumble on the team on a quest in Pangaea and would be terribly confused. The scientists would be equally confused when they encountered the Garou (if they do not end up gibbering in fear).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done pretty much this exact story hook. It was a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057261#post1057261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How do <i>you</i> want them to get to Pangea? Do you want it to have been convoluted, involving magick or the aid of other supernaturals? Or do you want a group of surveyors to stumble upon a hidden gateway into a distant realm, misunderstand what they have found, and start trying to take advantage of their circumstances? What makes for a better story, in your mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. Once the ST has decided this is what's going to happen, the rest are just details to sort out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T16:02:58-08:00","id":1057304,"title":"","content":"Yes, I agree. If you have scientists discovering a Converter Gate (my term) to Pangaea that transforms life to ephemera and ephemera to life, you have something that everyone would be willing to kill for in WtA. The ability to rebirth extinct species (or to corrupt Pangaea) would be too great of a prize to leave in the hands of mortals. The only question is who takes possession of it and how can they defend it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T18:45:37-08:00","id":1057382,"title":"","content":"Well said senior or senora","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T18:53:55-08:00","id":1057387,"title":"","content":"Dude all of the ideas in this thread are golden","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T18:56:39-08:00","id":1057390,"title":"","content":"I came with a scenario for how they found a portal to Pangaea. They arrived on the island and immediately had survey teams head out and scout the island. They disappeared for a few days and the head scientist was about to send in a rescue squad when the surveyors suddenly came back. They told about walking into a cave and finding themselves in a lush field. When they tried to go back through the cave, they found only a wall of stone. So they ended up stranded in this field for three days until the cave finally opened up. They also brought back some samples, which were mostly some apples and a clover.<br /> <br /> The Botanist in charge of the program decided to investigate this cave himself and went with the surveyors along with a security guard and three scientists to this &quot; miracle cave&quot;. Once they arrived, the Head Botanist went in the cave along with the security guard and the two other scientists, and disappeared for a week. Once they came back, they conformed the surveyors description of the filed and brought back more samples. This discovery has caused many more expeditions into Pangaea. It is a miracle they haven't run into any Fera or Spirit yet.<br /> <br /> Also, I was thinking about a adding a drone to the staff as head of security.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T18:57:08-08:00","id":1057391,"title":"","content":"How would you play a Converter Gate to Pangaea <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12902_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12902\" data-vbnamecard=\"12902\">WISDOMINCHAINS</a>? I would make it into the focal point of an entire arc of campaigns, as it would possible be the key to preventing the Apocalypse (or the key for causing the Apocalypse). Would a Converter Gate to Pangaea be something that you would find interesting for your game <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12186\" data-vbnamecard=\"12186\">Killerclown</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T18:58:17-08:00","id":1057393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057391#post1057391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you play a Converter Gate to Pangaea <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12902_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12902\" data-vbnamecard=\"12902\">WISDOMINCHAINS</a>? I would make it into the focal point of an entire arc of campaigns, as it would possible be the key to preventing the Apocalypse (or the key for causing the Apocalypse). Would a Converter Gate to Pangaea be something that you would find interesting for your game <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12186\" data-vbnamecard=\"12186\">Killerclown</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, in fact i wrote a explanation for how they discovered it in the post above you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T19:34:43-08:00","id":1057406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057391#post1057391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> as it would possible be the key to preventing the Apocalypse (or the key for causing the Apocalypse).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more than a bit overstated. It's a fun idea, but it will neither prevent or cause the Apocalypse (without much more interesting/dire things going on).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057390#post1057390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I came with a scenario for how they found a portal to Pangaea. They arrived on the island and immediately had survey teams head out and scout the island. They disappeared for a few days and the head scientist was about to send in a rescue squad when the surveyors suddenly came back. They told about walking into a cave and finding themselves in a lush field. When they tried to go back through the cave, they found only a wall of stone. So they ended up stranded in this field for three days until the cave finally opened up. They also brought back some samples, which were mostly some apples and a clover.<br /> <br /> The Botanist in charge of the program decided to investigate this cave himself and went with the surveyors along with a security guard and three scientists to this &quot; miracle cave&quot;. Once they arrived, the Head Botanist went in the cave along with the security guard and the two other scientists, and disappeared for a week. Once they came back, they conformed the surveyors description of the filed and brought back more samples. This discovery has caused many more expeditions into Pangaea. <u>It is a miracle they haven't run into any Fera or Spirit yet</u>.<br /> <br /> Also, I was thinking about a adding a drone to the staff as head of security.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a solid story or chronicle idea.<br /> Commenting on the line I underlined from the quote above: Fera aren't swarming over Pangea, so not encountering them isn't too odd. And it's a Realm, so it it as large as you need it to be (meaning the chance of running across anything you don't need for your story can be miniscule).<br /> On the spirit side, it is less black and white. There could be a discussion of emanations vs spirits, but personally I just used emanations and treated them as physical beings for all intents and purposes. And you can very easily have the scientists never encounter outside spirits so you don't really need to worry about the scientists having to deal with possible talking wind. For them, they really are in a past time, dealing with extinct species of plants (and very probably animals).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T19:47:51-08:00","id":1057411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057406#post1057406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is more than a bit overstated. It's a fun idea, but it will neither prevent or cause the Apocalypse (without much more interesting/dire things going on).<br /> <br /> <br /> Sounds like a solid story or chronicle idea.<br /> Commenting on the line I underlined from the quote above: Fera aren't swarming over Pangea, so not encountering them isn't too odd. And it's a Realm, so it it as large as you need it to be (meaning the chance of running across anything you don't need for your story can be miniscule).<br /> On the spirit side, it is less black and white. There could be a discussion of emanations vs spirits, but personally I just used emanations and treated them as physical beings for all intents and purposes. And you can very easily have the scientists never encounter outside spirits so you don't really need to worry about the scientists having to deal with possible talking wind. For them, they really are in a past time, dealing with extinct species of plants (and very probably animals).</div> </div> </div> </div>I could picture their reactions if they run into a dodo bird. One will probably to rationalize it saying it is a bird very similar to it while another will spout some kind of dumb theory about time travel. There will also probably be that guy who wants to kill and eat the dodo because they are stranded there for another week. Also, if they do run into a outside spirit, they would probably freak out and flee or be very curious. Not sure how the spirit would react.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T19:57:23-08:00","id":1057413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057411#post1057411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I could picture their reactions if they run into a dodo bird. One will probably to rationalize it saying it is a bird very similar to it while another will spout some kind of dumb theory about time travel. There will also probably be that guy who wants to kill and eat the dodo because they are stranded there for another week.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a range of human reactions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Ultimately, this portion of it seems like it will be entirely off screen so I wouldn't worry too much about it (though it is admittedly fun to run through mentally).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057411#post1057411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, if they do run into a outside spirit, they would probably freak out and flee or be very curious. Not sure how the spirit would react.</div> </div> </div> </div>This wholly depends on the spirit in question. There is an okay chance that the scientists don't even notice it. Most elemental spirits will move about with the scientists none the wiser. Animals spirits could just be an odd or out of place animal moving through. It's the weird spirits that will really stick out. A mobile (and seemingly sentient) color ribbon will raise more than a few flags for the stranded team, not that there would be much they could really do about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T20:19:34-08:00","id":1057421,"title":"","content":"They might think it was a hallucination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T20:34:22-08:00","id":1057425,"title":"","content":"Spirits being a hallucination is a great explanation for the scientists to use. Now, I am picturing how Garou would react. A Glasswalker, Uktena or Stargazer would be curious about how a bunch of humans got there and investigate. A Child of Gaia would currently be interested and would want to talk to the scientists. A Red Talon, Black Fury, or Get would probably be pissed . Not sure how Silver Fangs, Bone Gnawers, Wendigo or Shadow Lord would react.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T20:38:56-08:00","id":1057426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057421#post1057421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might think it was a hallucination.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's fairly likely conclusion. It would still be a jarring experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T20:55:28-08:00","id":1057435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057425#post1057425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits being a hallucination is a great explanation for the scientists to use. Now, I am picturing how Garou would react. A Glasswalker, Uktena or Stargazer would be curious about how a bunch of humans got there and investigate. A Child of Gaia would currently be interested and would want to talk to the scientists. A Red Talon, Black Fury, or Get would probably be pissed . Not sure how Silver Fangs, Bone Gnawers, Wendigo or Shadow Lord would react.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I think the reactions will vary a lot based on the players you have. The Talons are the only ones I think I would generalize into a they'd be pissed category.<br /> <br /> Slight tangent: So this was actually how it happened in the game I set up: First, the players played scientists from the future that were sent back in time because everything in the future had kind of gone to hell (this was a storyline lifted from a show called Terra Nova). They thought they were sent back to an alternate timeline. The Players play through the trials of carving out a new life in the prehistoric past. The alternate timeline idea also explains why some of the animals and plants are out of place.<br /> <br /> Next part of the game, we skip to the Garou PCs. They were sent on an Umbral quest to retrieve something from Pangea for an Elder. They stumble across the settlers (scientists and security, but mostly families) and have to figure out what the hell is going on. They sneak in and pretend to be part of the settlement and find out about the time travel thing. All of the players at least were really interested and the characters had different reactions. Only 1 of them wanted to slaughter the humans to rid Pangea of them.<br /> (later on the PCs find out that the settlers are emanations from the CyberRealm setting up a colony in Pangea, but all of the emanations completely believe the time travel story)<br /> <br /> So back on topic: I think the Garou reaction to something like this isn't so clear cut. Humans gaining (somewhat unique) access to Pangea isn't world ending. But it is something they will have to put thought into for a solution. Knee jerk reactions don't do anyone any good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T21:07:37-08:00","id":1057438,"title":"","content":"You make a good point. I would think that most Garou would probably be curious or confused. I also came up with a consequence if one pc gets all Crinos friendly and charges down the hill towards the scientists. The scientists see you coming, freak out and flee back to the cave, under the effect of the Delirium. Luckily for them, the portal back to the station opened and they blindly run back to the Material Plane. Unfortunately, the portal closes after that and the crinos, in a blind rage, runs into the cave wall.<br /> <br /> Sorry if that seemed cartoonish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T21:24:18-08:00","id":1057446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057438#post1057438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You make a good point. I would think that most Garou would probably be curious or confused. I also came up with a consequence if one pc gets all Crinos friendly and charges down the hill towards the scientists. The scientists see you coming, freak out and flee back to the cave, under the effect of the Delirium. Luckily for them, the portal back to the station opened and they blindly run back to the Material Plane. Unfortunately, the portal closes after that and the crinos, in a blind rage, runs into the cave wall.<br /> <br /> Sorry if that seemed cartoonish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without the running into the wall thing, this works as a completely serious scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T21:32:34-08:00","id":1057448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057446#post1057446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without the running into the wall thing, this works as a completely serious scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I guess the whole rage would be a problem long after the scientists disappear. I can just picture a Garou clawing at the wall while howling with rage, thinking the scientists are behind it. I think it would lead to a argument in the pack and leave the Garou wondering where the men in lab coats went.<br /> <br /> Also, I am wondering what would happen if the scientists try to bring a animal with them back from Pangaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T22:02:48-08:00","id":1057454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057448#post1057448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Really? I guess the whole rage would be a problem long after the scientists disappear. I can just picture a Garou clawing at the wall while howling with rage, thinking the scientists are behind it. I think it would lead to a argument in the pack and leave the Garou wondering where the men in lab coats went.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're Garou, not animals. They'll figure out what's going on at least somewhat quickly, even if they won't know the exact rules of the portal. I'm not entirely convinced of the Frenzy thing, though anger and assault in Crinos is a distinct possibility which still leads to the scientists running away with the cave closing behind them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1056425-would-this-be-weaver-or-wyld-tainted?p=1057448#post1057448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, I am wondering what would happen if the scientists try to bring a animal with them back from Pangaea.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one is entirely up to you. Decide for yourself whether the emanations have enough staying power to exist in the material world. And if they do, for how long (it could very well be indefinite). For your New Eden planting project, you kind of need the emanations to be able to stick around though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T07:10:09-08:00","id":1057582,"title":"","content":"Yes, that would be the promise of a Converter Gate (and the danger). The utility of a place like the Desolation Islands is that they are so remote and so uninhabited that the random dinosaur walking out of the portal would not be noticed (and would likely die of exposure long before it died of starvation). Of course, that could be the reason why the portal was discovered, when a biologist assigned to the Desolation Islands during the summer finds a living <i><b>Compsognathus longipes</b></i>(or other small dinosaur) foraging on dead fish on the shore of the main island.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T18:44:09-08:00","id":1057865,"title":"","content":"I guess a emanation could survive outside the Umbra. I already planned what happens after the scientists flee. All the PCs find from the scientists campsite is a scrap of clothing with a rainbow on it. When they get back to the Material Plane, they ask one of their elders if he recognizes the symbol and the elder points them out to a kinfolk who reveals the symbol to be a logo of a Agricultural company named Prism. They meet with the kinfolk and a buddy of his, who is a employee of Prism. The buddy tells them about the research facility but, before he could tell them where it is, he suddenly dies. It is revealed later that someone slipped poison in his coffee. After a bit of investigation and possibly a few run ins with Prism employees. They find out the location of the facility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}